1
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:24,760
What did you think of others when you were told that you have ADD or ADHD

2
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:30,520
What was the first thought?
-It was both a relief and "damn!"

3
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:37,640
Then you fall into their "you are a diagnosis child".

4
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:43,800
Did you tell people around, or did you hold it to yourself

5
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:51,360
In the beginning, I became worried about whether it would affect me in working life.

6
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:54,920
"Will people think I'm stupid"

7
00:09:55,080 --> 00:10:02,440
Once you say it to someone, they can speak this way:

8
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:06,080
"ADD, ie the disability"

9
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:10,120
What "disability"

10
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:16,840
You get a stamp, but I just have a little difficulty with the concentration.

11
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:23,600
They say, "Why can't you sit still and don't blame your ADHD."

12
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:21,640
I needed someone sitting next to it and wrote down the steps I would take.

13
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:27,320
Did you feel any change when you had received your diagnosis

14
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:30,520
For me it has been as before.

15
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:37,080
I have not received anything positive from it more than I know for myself what I have.

16
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:42,400
What would you like your teachers to do

17
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:48,920
I need someone who understands me and who is genuine and trying to help

18
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:52,080
And not just say "you have ADHD".

19
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:58,400
Now we will talk myths and claims about ADD and ADHD.
There are some

20
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:04,360
As we were going to test with you now.
We run "fact pingis".

21
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:14,840
Clara comes in with ping pong rackets to you all.

22
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:19,880
You see that it says "true" and "false" on them.

23
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:39,880
Sorry.
-"You better explain!"

24
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:46,000
“You can't ...“ Decide.
"You can't get it later in life."

25
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:51,640
You change your mind.
-That was what I meant.

26
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:56,360
Can anyone explain?
-It's...

27
00:16:56,520 --> 00:17:01,520
There is no age limit for when you can get it.

28
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:07,240
It's about your psyche.
It develops in your brain.

29
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:12,760
It can come with age.
-Add and adhd are born with.

30
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:19,400
It can trigger, so you end up in investigation when you are older

31
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:24,280
But ADD and ADHD you are born with.

32
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:30,720
Can anyone pick up ... I don't have the sources.
We can find out later.

33
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:36,000
Write the sources down here, so people can read.
